# V5.75: FIX fullscreen landscape - old code requested fullscreen on the DIV which fails in in-app WebViews and on HTTP. New: (1) tries native fullscreen on the VIDEO element itself (works on mobile), (2) webkitEnterFullscreen for iOS, (3) CSS fallback .lvfullscreen (fixed inset:0, 100vw/100vh, object-fit:contain) so it fills the screen even if the browser blocks the Fullscreen API. Exits free-float first.
# V5.74: (1) Removed Chrome, PiP and Background buttons - only Free Screen + Fullscreen Landscape remain per user request. (2) New Fullscreen Landscape button: requestFullscreen on lvbox + screen.orientation.lock(landscape), exit on second tap + unlock. (3) Free screen kept compact with drag bar + X + resize grip.
# V5.73: Fix Open in Chrome - old intent:// broke when URL had # fragment, when opened from in-app WebView (FB/WhatsApp/Meta AI blocks intents), or when Chrome was not default. New: (1) strips # fragment before building intent, (2) tries googlechrome:// first then intent:// with S.browser_fallback_url, (3) detects if already in Chrome and says so instead of trying to reopen and disconnecting, (4) if Chrome still does not open, shows the full URL to copy-paste manually instead of leaving the user with a disconnected app.
# V5.72: Auto-reconnect for Chrome disconnected - when the stream drops (error/stalled/waiting/no-data for 5s) it retries startLive automatically up to 8 times, with status "بيرجع لوحده". Same video element is reused so PiP stays alive across reconnects. Manual pause sets _lvManualStop so it does not fight the user.
# V5.71: Background playback - new "تشغيل في الخلفية" toggle. When ON: (1) the moment the app/page is hidden (Home / switch app), it auto-enters system PiP so the floating window pops up by itself and keeps playing; (2) Media Session is set so Android shows a media notification and keeps the audio alive; (3) on hide it re-calls play() so the browser does not pause the stream. This is the only way a web page can keep playing when minimized - via system PiP + media session.
# V5.70: Compact free screen - box is now exactly the video size (280px, no padding, no big header/buttons). Drag bar is a slim 26px overlay on top of the video that auto-hides after 3s (tap video to show it again), close is a tiny X. Double-tap video toggles small/big. Note: free screen lives INSIDE the browser so it hides when the browser is minimized - only system PiP (نافذة عايمة فوق التطبيقات) survives minimizing.
# V5.69: PiP fix - the PiP button used to fail because the video was still inside free-float (position:fixed) which Chrome rejects for PiP. Now it exits free-float first, then requests system PiP - the exact floating window over home screen / other apps the user showed in the screenshot. If the browser still refuses, it tells the guaranteed fallback: fullscreen + Home button makes Chrome show the same floating window automatically.
# V5.68: FIX - free screen button was floating the wrong element: it targeted #lvplayer which is just a small status-text line, not the video. Video wrapper now has id #lvbox and the free-screen button floats THAT. This is why the button appeared to do nothing.
# V5.67: New "شاشة حرة" - free floating video window inside the Panel: draggable by header, resizable by corner grip, minimize/maximize, stays on top while browsing channels/commentary/subtitles. Works in ANY browser (even in-app WebView) - no PiP API, no HTTPS needed. PiP button renamed "تعويم فوق التطبيقات": PiP floats over OTHER apps (needs Chrome), free screen floats inside the Panel.
# V5.66: (1) Removed the external-player (VLC) feature entirely - button, panel, JS funcs, /live/m3u, and all VLC mentions in messages. (2) PiP fixed properly: the old async retry lost the tap gesture (Chrome expires it after ~5s), so PiP now runs synchronously inside the tap when frames exist (play + float in one gesture); if no frames yet it starts playback and asks for one more tap once the picture appears. (3) New "افتح في Chrome" button - PiP only works in a real browser (Chrome); if the Panel was opened inside another app's built-in browser, PiP is blocked there, so this jumps to Chrome where PiP is guaranteed.
# V5.65: fix VLC + PiP. (1) VLC button now STOPS the browser player first (frees the 8001 connection - Enigma2 can refuse a 2nd client while the browser holds it), waits 800ms, then opens VLC on the direct URL; plus a new plain "🔗 افتح الرابط مباشرة" link as an intent-free fallback. (2) PiP button now starts playback itself if the video is not playing, waits until frames appear, then floats it; if PiP is rejected it shows the real error name and points to VLC (which floats natively) as the guaranteed fallback.
# V5.64: (1) VLC now opens the DIRECT receiver URL (http://HOST:8001/REF) instead of the Panel proxy (/live/stream) - the proxy PAT/PMT injection + delay queue made VLC drop with "disconnected"; direct is the native Enigma2 URL VLC expects. (2) New "بث عايم (PiP)" button - Picture-in-Picture floating video, so the user can open another app while the stream keeps playing on top.
# V5.63: smoother playback (player-only). (1) Drop the hw-decode attempt (_dec5 / hevc_v4l2m2m) + its 10s ffprobe pre-check - V4.99 used plain software decode and started instantly; on weak receivers the v4l2m2m decoder can stall/slow live HEVC. (2) Default transcode (تلقائي) now caps at 720p (1280) instead of 1080p - half the pixels to encode, much easier on the receiver CPU; FHD 1080 button still gives full 1920.
# V5.62: restore V4.99 player behaviour (player-only). (1) startLive transcodes ONLY for MPEG-2/H.265 again - the V5.61 quality buttons (FHD/HD) no longer force a transcode on H.264 channels, so H.264 plays direct TS like V4.99. Quality buttons still set the transcode resolution when a transcode IS needed. (2) encoder probe smoke tests back to V4.99 light sizes (64x64/0.2s) for VP8 and H.264 - V5.61 used 320x240/0.5s (VP8) and 720x576 (H.264) which time out on weak receiver CPUs, so the probe wrongly reported "no ffmpeg encoder" and fell back to the slow gstreamer VP8 that stutters. Now ffmpeg libvpx/libx264 is detected correctly and used first; gstreamer stays as last resort.
# V5.61: hide the status text under the video (lvstat box). The box is display:none by default so Live TV shows only the video + buttons. A 500ms watcher re-shows it automatically only for errors (خطأ/فشل/عدّى/مش بيرد/مشكلة/وقف/مفيش قناة/مفيش ترجمة) and confirmations (اتسجّل/اتحفظت/شغالة/❌/⚠️). Diagnose pins it visible; any play/stop unpins it. Normal status ("بيشغّل: /live/stream?ref=...") stays hidden.
# V5.60: gstreamer stutter fix. VP8 software encode at 720p was too heavy for the receiver CPU (buffer starved, spinner, cuts). gstreamer VP8 now uses a light profile: 854x480, videorate 20fps, vp8enc deadline=1000 cpu-used=10 target-bitrate=800k. gstreamer H.264: software x264enc gets the same light profile (480p/20fps/800k); hardware encoders (v4l2h264enc/omxh264enc) keep 720p. gstreamer watchdogs now wait 20s (not 12s) because the light encoder still starts slower than ffmpeg, avoiding the false "no picture" alarm seen when the video started just after the watchdog fired.
# V5.59: gstreamer as a second transcoder (besides ffmpeg). Server probes gst-launch-1.0 for an MPEG-2 decoder + H.264 encoders (v4l2h264enc hardware, omxh264enc hardware, x264enc) or vp8enc, returns it as "gst" in the transcode probe. Client falls back to gstreamer (fmt=gst-h264 / gst-vp8) when ffmpeg has no H.264 and no VP8, in startLive, the TS watchdog and lvTryTranscode. gstreamer path is video-only (channel audio comes from commentary or VLC). Diagnose reports gstreamer too.
# V5.58: Live TV is 8001 ONLY. Removed the 8002 button, setQ, the 8002 direct branch and the 8002->8001 auto-switch from the client, and the server now forces port 8001 in every Live TV handler (stream/check/transcode/subs/m3u) ignoring any port param. VP8 fallback (V5.57) kept.
# V5.57: VP8 smoke test tries 2 variants (with/without deadline+cpu-used) and the real VP8 transcode reuses the proven args + caps at 720p for real-time CPU encode. VP8 fallback added to startLiveTS watchdog and lvTryTranscode (was only in startLive). checkStream(auto): when the auto check on 8002 fails (e.g. Connection refused) it switches to 8001 immediately instead of waiting 12s.
# V5.56: rely on receiver ports 8002/8001. Default 8002 (receiver hardware transcode -> H.264, no ffmpeg needed). Two port buttons 8002-خفيف / 8001-أصلي. 8002 path skips ffprobe+ffmpeg entirely and plays direct; if 8002 gives no picture in 12s+delay it auto-switches to 8001. VLC direct URL, VLC intent and m3u download all follow the selected port.
# V5.55: "IT WAS WORKING" - diffed V5.27 (working) vs V5.54. Two regressions found and fixed: (1) JS watchdogs declared "no picture" after 12s even when picture-delay was set - now they wait 12s + delay. (2) V5.54 forced hardware HEVC decode with no fallback - now if hw decode yields no output, the transcode retries with software decode (V5.27 behaviour). Direct TS path with delay=0 is byte-identical to V5.27, so H.264 channels were never broken by the script - if an H.264 channel fails, the channel changed or the receiver is not streaming.
# V5.54: STOP GUESSING - added one-tap "Diagnose" button on Live TV that checks /version + /live/check + ffmpeg probe in sequence and prints a plain-language verdict: is the server alive, is the receiver streaming, what codec, does ffmpeg have an encoder, and the direct VLC URL. Cache headers, kill-on-start, and ThreadingHTTPServer were all verified already present - the update path is NOT the problem.
# V5.53: STREAM STILL NOT WORKING - made playback bulletproof with 3 independent paths. (1) VLC button now opens a panel with the DIRECT stream URL visible + Copy URL + download m3u + intent - if any one fails, copy the URL into VLC manually (VLC -> More -> Open network stream -> paste). (2) NEW "Try transcode anyway" button bypasses the ffmpeg probe - if the probe falsely reports "no encoder", the real transcode is attempted and the REAL ffmpeg error is shown from the transcode log instead of a generic message. Server already ThreadingHTTPServer - not a blocking issue.
# V5.52: RESTORED V4.99 VLC. Diagnosis from V4.99 file: V4.99 VLC was a plain <a href="/live/m3u"> link (download m3u -> open in VLC) and THAT is what worked; V5.05 changed VLC to an intent:// URL to the U-Panel proxy which silently fails if VLC is not installed or the intent is blocked. Restored the plain m3u link. ALSO: ffmpeg probe smoke tests now use 720x576 instead of 64x64 - hardware encoders (h264_v4l2m2m) can reject tiny frames and were falsely reported as "no encoder". Playback code itself is IDENTICAL between V4.99 and V5.51 - no playback regression.
# V5.51: DIAGNOSIS FIX - "nothing works" was invisible. (1) lvstat moved to directly under the video player, big + bold, so Play/Check/VLC results are always visible (it was at the bottom of the card, below the fold). (2) srvver watchdog: if /version still pending after 5s, show "server not responding - check receiver is on + same WiFi + reload page" in red instead of hanging on "checking..." forever. (3) startLive check watchdog: if /live/check hangs >10s, show a clear message. (4) openVLC: if VLC did not open, lvstat now says VLC may not be installed or play the downloaded m3u manually. (5) /version falls back to the real version instead of "?". (6) stale hardcoded V5.26 badges in Live TV header + subtitles card fixed to the real version.
# V5.50: Live TV quality selector - Auto / FHD 1080 / HD 720 buttons under Play/Stop. Picking FHD or HD FORCES the ffmpeg transcode path (even if codec check would have used direct TS) and caps the scale: 720 -> max 1280 wide (much lighter encode, more likely to play smooth on the receiver CPU), 1080/auto -> max 1920 wide as before. All transcode URLs (H.264, VP8 fallback, retry paths) carry &q=. Server /live/transcode accepts q=720.
# V5.49: FIX 4K streaming + 4K screenshot. Root cause: 4K = HEVC decoded in SOFTWARE on the receiver ARM CPU + software x264 encode - cannot keep up in realtime, so the player stays black and canvas screenshot has nothing to capture. Fix: (1) probe + use hevc_v4l2m2m hardware HEVC decoder when input is HEVC; (2) prefer h264_v4l2m2m hardware H.264 encoder first (smoke-tested, falls back to libx264); (3) new /live/shot endpoint grabs ONE frame server-side via ffmpeg (max 1280 wide JPEG) so screenshot works even when live playback stalls; lvShot falls back to it when the video element is not playing or canvas capture is blocked.
# V5.48: FIX tamper re-seal infinite loop - _lock_seal_tmp now VERIFIES the seal line was actually written (sed no-match used to return success, commit saved an unsealed file, restart asked PIN again forever). Tamper choice 2 now fails loudly with the obfuscation explanation instead of looping. Obfuscated copies can never be re-sealed - use the clean file.
