# V4.43: Fixed lamedb matching - it was reading the fields in the wrong order, so NO channel ever matched and everything stayed "Unnamed channel". Real format is SID:NS:TSID:ONID (not SID:TSID:ONID:NS). lamedb5 services are one line each (s:SID:NS:TSID:ONID:STYPE:0:0,"Name",p:Provider), lamedb services are three lines (SID:NS:TSID:ONID:... / Name / p:Provider). Verified against the user's own lamedb + lamedb5 (8221 / 8136 services): MBC1, Madrastna 1, Al Hadath now resolve.
# V4.42: IPTV channels are NOT in lamedb, so they stayed "Unnamed channel". Added a third name source: for IPTV service refs the name is now read from the stream link itself (last part of the URL, decoded, e.g. "MBC Egypt", "beIN SPORTS 1 HD"). Also accepts the "#DESCRIPTION:" (colon) variant some IPTV bouquets use, in list / rename / delete. Display order is now: #DESCRIPTION in bouquet, then lamedb, then IPTV link name, then "Unnamed channel".
# V4.41: Channel names now also come from the channel database (lamedb / lamedb5 in /etc/enigma2). Display order: #DESCRIPTION in the bouquet first, then the name from lamedb matched by service ref (SID/TSID/ONID/namespace), then "Unnamed channel". Applies to the bouquet page, Timers/EPG dropdowns, Timers list, EPG alerts form and alerts list. Rename now also works on channels without #DESCRIPTION: it inserts the #DESCRIPTION line instead of silently doing nothing.
# V4.40: Channel names everywhere in the Panel UI - no service codes shown. Bouquet page shows the channel name only (no grey #SERVICE line), channels without a name show "Unnamed channel", bouquet page title and bouquet list use the bouquet name (from #DESCRIPTION in bouquets.tv, or #NAME inside the bouquet file as fallback), Timers list shows the channel name, Timers/EPG dropdowns show name only. EPG alerts show the channel name too: in the alert form and in the alerts list. Service codes stay internal only (hidden values / XML), so Rename/Delete/Timers/Zap still work. Virtual Remote made smaller (320px wide, smaller buttons and gaps).
