# V4.38: Virtual Remote - removed the green "OpenWebif is reachable" banner. When the remote works, the page now opens straight on the remote with no status text. The warning banners stay: NOT installed (with one-click install) and installed-but-not-answering (restart Enigma) - those only show when something is actually wrong.
# V4.37: Screenshot added INSIDE the Virtual Remote (not on the Panel) - a full-width SCREENSHOT button at the bottom of the remote. /screenshot shows the live receiver screen with "Take new screenshot" + "Back to remote". /screenshot.png grabs via OpenWebif (/grab then /web/grab), falling back to the grab tool writing /tmp/upanel-shot.png. No extra Panel clutter - the screenshot lives where you are already driving the box.
# V4.36: Virtual Remote - no more "Sent key" message page. Pressing a key now sends it and silently redirects straight back to the remote (302 to /remote), so you can press key after key like a real remote. Redesign: every button has its own color - red POWER/REC, orange MUTE, cyan INFO, purple MENU, pink EPG, blue UP, teal DOWN, amber LEFT, violet RIGHT, green round OK, light/dark blue volume, magenta/indigo channel, each digit 1-9 its own color, real red/green/yellow/blue color keys, green PLAY / yellow PAUSE / red STOP.
# V4.35: Panel UI Virtual Remote fixed + redesigned. Root cause: the remote sends keys through OpenWebif - if OpenWebif is not installed, nothing happens. The remote page now self-checks OpenWebif (plugin folder + live answer), shows a clear status banner (reachable / installed-but-not-answering / NOT installed), offers one-click OpenWebif install (opkg enigma2-plugin-extensions-openwebif) and a Diagnosis page, and /remote/send now tries both /web/remotecontrol and /api/remotecontrol before reporting failure. Redesign: colored remote - red POWER/REC, green round OK, gray nav pad, blue volume, purple channel, gray digits, real red/green/yellow/blue color keys, teal media keys (mute/play/pause/stop).
# V4.34: Panel UI gains 4 pages - Recording Timers (list / add by channel+date+duration / delete, Enigma stopped while saving timers.xml), Plugin Manager (installed Extensions list / delete folder / install + search feeds via opkg), Receiver Status (uptime, temp, memory, disk, load, tuner signal, timers/plugins/backups counts), Virtual Remote (keypad + nav + color keys via OpenWebif). Plus: Scheduled Backup (weekly/daily cron from the Panel UI, runs Backup Ur Data/Files while you sleep), Telegram Notifications (bot token + chat ID in Panel UI, message on backup/restore/flash/update finish; scheduled cron runs notify from the shell), Disk Cleanup (timeshift / crash logs / incomplete downloads / old backups over 30 days, each with confirm).
# V4.33: Remote Access (Cloudflare Tunnel) REMOVED - Panel UI is LAN-only again. No outgoing tunnel, no public link, nothing leaves the home network. Panel Control works only on the home WiFi (or a VPN you set up yourself on the router).
# V4.31: Panel Control gains Listen Address (Bind IP) - choose which network the Panel UI listens on: All interfaces (0.0.0.0, default) / LAN IP only / VPN IP only (Tailscale/WireGuard, auto-detected) / Localhost only / Custom IP. Saved in /etc/u-panel-web-bind.conf, applies on restart. Binding picks WHICH network listens - it does NOT create internet access; from outside home you still need a VPN or tunnel.
# V4.30: Panel Control gains - Channel Editor (list bouquets / rename + delete channel / create bouquet / renew channel list, backup before every edit, Enigma stopped during edits), Download Image (paste direct .zip link, list / delete downloaded images), Flash Image to Slot (pick image + slot, type FLASH, running slot refused, uses upanel_flash via --web-flash), Image Update on current slot (check updates / update now via opkg/apt, no flash). New headless flags --web-flash / --web-channellist-renew.
